<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (At first glance, the question "What is communication?" might seem straightforward. However, communication is one of the most intricate and multifaceted concepts in human existence. It involves not just the exchange of words, but a complex interaction of various elements.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (There are 195 countries in the world, but over 7,139 known languages, with more being discovered regularly. This number doesn't include the myriad of dialects, which are variations within a language. For example, the English language alone boasts over 150 dialects. This complexity is further compounded by the ways people personalize their language.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
