/E (Two teens found themselves in a heated texting fight. Words were being shot back and forth at a rapid pace. So quickly were the responses, one would wonder if either stopped to truly read each other's texts. Finally, one of the parents, noticing how flustered the other was, jumped in to inquire. As the teen began to explain, an issue concerning going to the movies quickly turned into an argument about how one person never thinks of the other. The conversation evolved into a fiery disagreement. But, as the mom reflected on the conversation, she quickly spotted how it got off track. It had to do with misunderstanding. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
